  "_note": "How every SDK reads a Retry-After header (conformance/README.md). `seconds`: honoured as the wait when it is at most 30; `surface`: a number above the 30 s cap, or too large to represent: raise Unavailable at once with retryAfterSeconds set (capped at 86400), NEVER retry early; `ignored`: not a plain decimal number of seconds (an HTTP date, garbage, a hex or suffixed form): treated as no header, the normal backoff applies. Syntax of a number: an optional +, digits, an optional fraction (.5 and 5. are both decimals: 0.5 s and 5 s; a lone . is not), an optional exponent (e or E, optional sign), nothing else; or Inf / Infinity in any case (an infinite wait is the longest one). Every SDK runs these in its own tests.",
